language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ revenue_maximization: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ We have a set of flight legs, each one-way non-stop, with a limited passenger capacity. A set of flight
$ itineraries is sold as packages, each at a given price, with an estimated demand. Each package uses some of the legs and
$ reserves seats on them. Find how many units of each package to sell so that the total revenue is as large as possible.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `revenue_maximization.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/revenue_maximization.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `revenue_maximization_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py revenue_maximization.json
$   savilerow model.eprime revenue_maximization_1.param -run-solver

$ demand_dim1: the number of packages (derived from the data)
given demand_dim1 : int
$ available_seats_dim1: the number of flight legs (derived from the data)
given available_seats_dim1 : int
$ demand[p]: the estimated demand for package p (indices from 1)
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..demand_dim1)] of int(0..)
$ revenue[p]: the price of package p
given revenue : matrix indexed by [int(1..demand_dim1)] of int(0..)
$ available_seats[l]: the passenger seats on leg l
given available_seats : matrix indexed by [int(1..available_seats_dim1)] of int(0..)
$ delta[p,l]: 1 when package p uses leg l, else 0 (indices from 1)
given delta : matrix indexed by [int(1..demand_dim1), int(1..available_seats_dim1)] of int(0..1)

$ packages_to_sell[p]: the number of units of package p to sell (indices from 1)
find packages_to_sell : matrix indexed by [int(1..demand_dim1)] of int(0..max(demand))
$ max_revenue: the total revenue of the units sold
find max_revenue : int(0..(sum p : int(1..demand_dim1) . revenue[p] * demand[p]))

maximising max_revenue
such that
$ no more units of a package are sold than its estimated demand
forAll p : int(1..demand_dim1) . packages_to_sell[p] <= demand[p],
$ the seats reserved on each leg do not exceed the seats available on it
forAll l : int(1..available_seats_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..demand_dim1) . delta[p,l] * packages_to_sell[p]) <= available_seats[l],
$ the revenue is the price of each package times the units sold
max_revenue = (sum p : int(1..demand_dim1) . revenue[p] * packages_to_sell[p])
